{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/657705-question-about-amara-havana-and-sakti-pata","id":657705,"title":"Question about Amara Havana and Sakti Pata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T05:22:31-07:00","id":657705,"title":"Question about Amara Havana and Sakti Pata","content":"Hi! Thanks in advance first!<br /> <br /> I\u00b4m a PC and we\u00b4ve been playing a requiem chronicle for a long time, now my Daeva joined the Amara Havana bloodline, we are starting to use the rules of Sakti Pata, but something doens't seen to be clear. If I use the first power &quot;Halahala&quot; to make my blood poisonous, but leave it in my system, them I use the second power &quot;Gift of Indra&quot; to make a weapon with that blood, it will poison on hit? Could you guys with more experience in lineages help with this one!?<br /> <br /> Best regards,<br /> Leonardo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2951-leosfa","name":"leosfa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T02:10:44-07:00","id":664057,"title":"","content":"Storyteller's discretion I believe.<br /> <br /> I would personally rule that it applied poison on hits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:20:17-07:00","id":664616,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply ManusDomine, that\u00b4s what i thought, especially because in the description it\u00b4s is said that is a &quot;semi-solid&quot; weapon, but both me and my storyteller think it could be a little game breaking, anyone already used that power of Sakti Pata in game? Any thoughts of the developers on this discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2951-leosfa","name":"leosfa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:58:51-07:00","id":664656,"title":"","content":"The developer on that book is still around, but a different person is the developer for Vampire as a whole.<br /> <br /> I would say as long as you spend the Vitae for Halahala as if the Gift of Indra weapon was a normal weapon then you are well within intent. I wouldn't let you shortcut out of the Vitae cost for poisoning a weapon. I wouldn't let you drink back the Vitae used for poisoning. In 2E, I would put a time limit on the effectiveness of the poison in or out of the body, scene on the weapon and until sunrise within the body or perhaps nights per blood potency. There should be no problems unless the poison doesn't use up Vitae to work outside of people drinking the vampire's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","